# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS (2026-09-10). Ben played a shift on a build that was two
# deploys old, hard-refreshed, and still had it — then spent an afternoon
# reporting a bug that had already been fixed, while every check I ran against
# the live site passed. The host sends NO Cache-Control on index.html, so
# browsers fall back to HEURISTIC caching (roughly a tenth of the file's age
# since last-modified) and quietly keep serving a stale document that points at
# stale bundle hashes. A hard refresh does not always beat it.
#
# index.html is the ONE file that must always be revalidated: it is the map to
# every hashed bundle. The bundles themselves are content-addressed
# (index-<hash>.js), so a name never means two different files and they can be
# cached forever.
<IfModule mod_headers.c>
  <FilesMatch "\.html$">
    Header set Cache-Control "no-cache, must-revalidate, max-age=0"
  </FilesMatch>
  <FilesMatch "\.(js|css|png|jpg|svg|woff2?)$">
    Header set Cache-Control "public, max-age=31536000, immutable"
  </FilesMatch>
</IfModule>
